#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/bretonnia.adoc:291
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/vampire-counts.adoc:242
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:193
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:42
msgid ""
"The unit can be moved just as if it had received an order in the Command "
"phase. Character stands that have joined the unit will not move with it: "
"they remain where they are."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/witch-hunters.adoc:226
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:64
msgid ""
"The unit moves at half pace in all situations: even when charging for "
"example. The unit counts all enemies as terrifying (−1 Attack penalty) even "
"when it is otherwise immune to terror. If the unit would normally cause "
"terror then it ceases to do so and counts all enemies as terrifying just "
"like everyone else. However, if the target is Undead or Daemon it will not "
"count enemies as terrifying although all other penalties apply as described "
"(Undead and Daemons are hard to spook)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ball of Flame"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:8
msgid ""
"_A ball of flame shoots form the Wizard’s outstretched arm burning all in "
"its path._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:14
msgid ""
"Draw an imaginary line 30cm long from the Wizard’s stand in any direction "
"you wish. The line will pass through any intervening units but not beyond "
"terrain that would normally stop a missile shot, e.g. over the crest of a "
"hill, more than 2cm of woodland, and so forth."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:24
msgid ""
"Each unit under the line takes three shooting attacks worked out in the "
"usual way. Note that this spell can easily affect several units and will "
"affect all units that fall beneath the line (including your own). Unengaged "
"units can be driven back by a Ball of Flame as with ordinary shooting (even "
"including friends). Engaged units cannot be driven back by the Ball of Flame "
"but carry over any hits scored into the first round of combat; any hits "
"scored count as having been struck in the combat itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:26
#, no-wrap
msgid "Voice of Command"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:33
msgid ""
"_The Wizard’s voice booms out across the battlefield directing troops above "
"the tumult of combat with the magical Voice of Command._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:38
msgid ""
"The spell can be cast on any unengaged friendly unit within range regardless "
"of whether the Wizard can see it or not. The spell affects only a single "
"unit, never a brigade and there is no supporting charge possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:44
#, no-wrap
msgid "Weird Enchantment"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:51
msgid ""
"_A weird enchantment forms around the target unit and engulfs it in strange "
"lights, scary nightmares and disorientating special effects._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:55
msgid ""
"This spell can be cast on any enemy unit within range regardless of whether "
"the Wizard can see it or not. The spell lasts until the end of the opposing "
"player’s following turn."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:66
#, no-wrap
msgid "Teleport"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:69
msgid "[.cost]#2+ to cast# [.points]#Range N/A#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:73
msgid ""
"_With a swirl of his cloak, a crack of thunder and just a hint of maniacal "
"laughter the Wizard vanishes to reappear anywhere on the battlefield._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/partials/empire-spells.adoc:80
msgid ""
"The Wizard is moved to a new position anywhere on the table.  He can leave "
"or join a unit if he wishes, enabling a Wizard to move into or out of combat "
"for example. Once the Wizard has moved he can cast a second spell, but note "
"this must be a different spell and not a further Teleport! Roll to cast the "
"second spell as normal. A Wizard that Teleports successfully can therefore "
"potentially cast two spells that turn."
msgstr ""
